<title>USA: UPS, Teamsters contract talks continuing - union.</title>
<headline>UPS, Teamsters contract talks continuing - union.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Just minutes before a midnight deadline,  Teamsters spokesman Rand Wilson said he had been told by union officials  negotiating with United Parcel Service that contract talks were continuing  and that union members should wait for further instructions.</p>
<p>&quot;Our members are waiting for instructions from the national negotiating  committee,&quot; Wilson told reporters at the Federal Mediation and Conciliation  Service, where the two sides are trying to avert a strike that would  cripple the nation's largest parcel carrier.</p>
<p>-- Washington newsroom, ((202-898-8300))</p>
</text>
